<p>
    <strong>Core Gameplan:</strong> This one swings hard on the play/draw.
    Your job is to protect your basic mana and keep hitting land drops while
    they blow up your lands
    (<a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Stone Rain"
        >Stone Rain</a
    >, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Pillage"
        >Pillage</a
    >). Mulligan shaky two-land hands that don't have basics or early
    filtering—you can't afford to stumble into their land destruction.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Sideboard Strategy:</strong> Cut fragile early creatures
    like <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a
    > for a real finisher (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a
    >). <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Tsabo's Web">Tsabo's Web</a
    > is a must—it shuts down their <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Rishadan Port">Rishadan Port</a
    > and <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Wasteland">Wasteland</a
    >. Even in builds running your own factories, the tax Web puts on
    them is worth more than the small hit to your own synergy.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Tactical Considerations:</strong> Keep at least 2–3
    copies of <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Swords to Plowshares"
        >Swords to Plowshares</a
    >; cut spot removal entirely and you leave yourself dead to
    a fast beater like <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Terravore">Terravore</a
    > or <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Ravenous Baluchitherium"
        >Ravenous Baluchitherium</a
    >. Think about your speed, too: some players keep <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Frantic Search">Frantic Search</a
    > to dig through their taxing effects, but trimming the pricier
    filtering usually makes your curve more consistent.<br />
    <em>Spicy tech:</em>
    <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Divert"
        >Divert</a
    > works as a pseudo-counter against their targeted land destruction, and
    <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Sacred Ground">Sacred Ground</a
    > shuts their whole destruction plan off completely.
</p>
